<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Bring up the Remote Control server so Nate can reach this checkout from the
  Claude mobile app. It starts a detached tmux session; tmux is parented to
  launchd rather than to the Claude desktop app, so the server survives quitting
  the app. Measured 2026-09-09: started inside the desktop app's terminal panel,
  `claude rc` dies with that panel's shell.

  This is a listener, not a schedule. It idles until Nate sends a message from a
  device and issues no prompt of its own; see the Remote Control carve-out in
  `AGENTS.md`, which is why this does not fall under the ban on invoking the
  Claude CLI from launchd.

  It fires at Nate's login, not at boot. Auto-login on this Mac goes to the
  `claude` account, so a LaunchAgent under `nateprich` cannot run any earlier;
  the alternative was enabling auto-login for this account, which writes a
  recoverable password to `/etc/kcpassword` and was rejected on 2026-09-09.

  The job is idempotent: it does nothing when the session already exists, so a
  reload never produces a second server. The brief sleep lets the login keychain
  unlock first; Remote Control needs the OAuth token and exits 1 without it.

  The canonical copy lives here in the repo. launchd refuses a symlinked plist
  (`Bootstrap failed: 5: Input/output error`, measured 2026-09-07), so the
  installed file is a copy and `tests/test_launchd_drift.py` compares them.

  Note for editors: XML forbids a double hyphen inside a comment. Use an em dash
  or a semicolon; plutil accepts the double hyphen and plistlib rejects it, so a
  file can lint clean and still be unparseable.

  After editing, re-install:
    cp launchd/com.nateprich.command-center-remote-control.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.nateprich.command-center-remote-control
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.nateprich.command-center-remote-control.plist
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.nateprich.command-center-remote-control</string>

    <!--
      `=rc` is an exact session match; a bare `rc` would also match `rc-anything`
      and silently skip starting the real one.
    -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/sh</string>
        <string>-c</string>
        <string>sleep 15; tmux has-session -t =rc || tmux new-session -d -s rc -x 200 -y 50 -c /Users/nateprich/.claude/command-center '/opt/homebrew/bin/claude rc --spawn=same-dir'</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/nateprich/Library/Logs/command-center-remote-control.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/nateprich/Library/Logs/command-center-remote-control.err.log</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/Users/nateprich/.local/bin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>/Users/nateprich</string>
    </dict>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>
